Subject: config.h: let <assert.h> define assert again on OpenVMS

For static_assert, gnulib's config.h includes <assert.h> and then
#undefs assert, relying on the program's own later #include <assert.h> to
define it again, as the C standard requires of <assert.h>.  VSI C's
<assert.h> is guarded by __ASSERT_LOADED, so the second inclusion did
nothing and every use of assert failed to compile.  Undefine the guard too.
The text comes from gnulib's m4/assert_h.m4, where the same change
belongs upstream.  (As in vms-wget.)

--- a/lib/config.hin	2026-10-05 02:51:41.907758733 +0100
+++ b/lib/config.hin	2026-10-05 02:51:56.206652107 +0100
@@ -3737,6 +3737,9 @@
  #ifdef __sgi
   #undef/**/__ASSERT_H__
  #endif
+ #ifdef __VMS
+  #undef/**/__ASSERT_LOADED
+ #endif
  /* Solaris 11.4 <assert.h> defines static_assert as a macro with 2 arguments.
     We need it also to be invocable with a single argument.
     Haiku 2022 <assert.h> does not define static_assert at all.  */
